**Objective.** We introduce a cosmological parameter constraint framework based on HI intensity mapping (HI IM) power spectrum multipoles.

**Methodology.** We adopt the three-dimensional Hi 21-cm power spectrum model, $P(k,z)$, as the foundation for the HI IM two-point correlation function. By utilizing analytic expressions for the correlation function, we derive closed-form equations for the multipole moments of the power spectrum, $P_\ell(k,z)$. These multipoles are integrated against the square of the top-hat window function to obtain the corresponding moments of the power spectrum, $P_\ell(k)$. By summing over a wavenumber bin, we construct the multipole moments of the HI IM configuration function, $P_{\ell}^{\rm{conf}}(k)$.

